<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Santa Maria del Mar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1329">1329</a>–1383</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Santa Maria del Mar is a Gothic basilica in the Ribera quarter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barcelona">Barcelona</a>, built between 1329 and 1383 with the support of the city's merchants and sailors. With its wide nave and slender octagonal pillars, it is the finest example of Catalan Gothic architecture.</p></div>
